  "id": "COMPOUND:21042 - PROTEIN:4892",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between the compound (2S)-1-O-3,6,9,12,15-Octadecapentaenoyl-2-O-6,9,12,15-Octadecatetraenoyl-3-O-Beta-D-Galactopyranosylsn-Glycerol and the CD70 antigen, mediated through the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This compound is identified as a target of multiple molecules, including (2R,3R,4S,5R)-2-(6-aminopurin-9-yl)-5-methanidyl-tetrahydrofuran-3,4-diol, 7,10-Octadecadienoic acid, methyl ester, and Glabrol. All of these molecules are known to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is a key component in the polycomb repressive complex 2 (PRC2) and is involved in epigenetic regulation. The CD70 antigen, a surface protein on B cells, is a known target of several compounds, including those that interact with the PRC2 complex. The evidence suggests that the compound in question may act as a modulator of the PRC2 complex, thereby influencing the expression of CD70 antigen. The strength of the evidence is moderate, as multiple pathways converge on the same target, but the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
